[76:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hacker OS, and why this is kind of my dream tool. Now, full disclosure, this is a tool that I\'ve developed, so I\'m obviously a little bit biased towards it, but I\'ve really done my best to try and make this the best tool for writers'

[76:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that I can. Because most of the tools out there for writers don\'t have any kind of automated system, and I am a big believer in those automated systems. But then the automated systems also have a problem because it makes it difficult to kind of use AI to fine-tune things, just'

[76:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'interact with the document like I could in Claude, for instance. So, this has been my answer to that as a way of kind of combining the best of both worlds. So, to give you a little bit of a tour, you have a document here in the center,'

[77:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and over here you have a chatbot. And this chatbot works very similar to what you would find in Claude, where it has access to this document and it has that context, and it can give you suggestions and things like that. Down here it also'

[77:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
