[152:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'focus more on those areas that bring you the most joy. That is the best marriage of technology with human creativity is to let the technology take care of what is drudgework for you, so you can focus'

[152:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'more on what is enjoyable for you. That way, not only does it make the whole process [music] more joyful for yourself, but I think that will also lead to a much better product at the end'

[152:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of this whole process. And [music] once again, the writing process is multiple steps. It\'s not just one thing. We\'ve literally spent probably hours at this point going through this whole process, and we\'re only now getting to the actual'

[153:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'writing part. Writing has always been a multi-step process, so there\'s a chance that at least one of those steps is one you don\'t enjoy that much. Use AI for that. Figure out which step of the process is your favorite, and do that'

[153:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'part yourself. The second concern I want to address is the idea of AI slop. Remember, it\'s only slop if it\'s bad. Human slop absolutely exists as well. In this case, AI helps with prose writing a'

[153:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ton, but effort is still required. This is about working smarter and harder, not just harder. Also, another concern, Amazon actually has no problem with AI-written text as long as the quality is good. They care more about the user'

[153:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'experience, which you should too, but you do have to disclose the use of AI to Amazon. They\'re the only people that I recommend you do disclose this to. To anybody worried that Amazon\'s going to de-list your book just because they used'

