[218:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Amazon. Next is territories. I just always select all territories. And then the primary marketplace, again, select whichever one is most relevant to you. And then you have pricing, royalty, and distribution. So, there are two options'

[218:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here. You can get the 35% royalty or the 70% royalty. And you might ask, why would anybody want to have the 35% royalty? Um most of the time you don\'t, but there are limits to'

[218:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what you can do at the 70% royalty. The big one is that you need to have a book that is priced between $2.99 and $9.99, uh at least with the US pricing. I don\'t'

[219:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'know exactly what it might be for other markets. So, it needs to be within that window, or you have to use 35. So, if you went and wanted to sell a book for $20, you\'d have to use the 35% royalty rate, which would actually be the same'

[219:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'amount of money coming to you as if you sold it for $10 at the 70% rate. Generally speaking, the most you want to charge for a book is 70 uh is $9.99 because that is the most you can get at'

[219:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the 70% range here. You could always sell a book for $100 and get 350 from that and get $35 from that sale at the 35% price, but it\'s just easier to stick to the 70 whenever possible. The only'

[219:46] [scene:talk]
